Research (Claude Code 2.1.330, released 2026-11-20): one class of their fixes carries over to yoyo. Settings were lost when several processes saved at once, and incomplete backups were kept when the disk was full. From reading the code only, yoyo writes .yoyo.toml and .yoyo/memory.json with a plain std::fs::write: no lock, and no write-to-temp-then-rename. My attempt to test this was void: yoyo config set from the shell refuses without an interactive session, so it tested the refusal, not the writer. I saved the comparison to yopedia.
